#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Chess: register a player, play 1. e4 e5, save the game as 'Game', and quit cleanly (#159).
# Extends throne-room.route through a two-player Western Quick Game: plays 1. e4 e5, opens the
# in-game Options menu, opens Save Game, clears the default '....' label in slot 1, types 'Game',
# confirms the save (writing profiles\1save.lcs), resigns cleanly back to the Quick Game screen,
# and closes the window cleanly (exited 0).
#
# Replay with a fresh `--data-root <empty dir>`, never beside the rip. It writes
# profiles\prof1.lcp (4,544 bytes) and profiles\1save.lcs (190,920 bytes), which
# routes/load-game.route reloads in a second run over the same `--data-root`.
#
# From flip 432 on the Quick Game screen:
# - (520,180) toggles Black from computer to human (flip 440, let go at poll 300).
# - (590,410) clicks the green tick to start the Western match (flip 450, let go at poll 300).
# - Plays 1. e2-e4 (White, flips 560..581) and 1... e7-e5 (Black, rotated view, flips 730..751).
#   By flip 895 the board has rotated back to White's view with both e-pawns on e4 and e5.
# - (200,60) opens the in-game Options menu (flip 905, let go at poll 300).
# - (282,258) opens the Save Game dialog with slot 1 highlighted (flip 925, let go at poll 300).
# - Four Backspaces (flips 936..957) clear '....', then Shift+G, a, m, e (flips 960..983) type
#   'Game' into slot 1's label box.
# - (392,194) clicks the Save Game green tick (flip 995, let go at poll 300), writing
#   profiles\1save.lcs (190,920 bytes, 10 x 19,092-byte slots) and returning to the board.
# - Escape (flip 1015, let go at poll 300) opens "Are you sure you want to resign?", and
#   (360,232) clicks its green tick (flip 1030, let go at poll 300), freeing the engine table and
#   returning to the Quick Game screen.
# - Closing the window at flip 1080 exits 0 cleanly.
